From a90249dd802273130baf972340b37107396f633f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:04:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Per-plate printers: let each plate use its own printer and
 process

A plate can name its own printer preset, and optionally its own process
preset, in the Plate Settings dialog. The plate is then drawn with that
printer's bed and sliced with that printer's settings, so one project can
hold plates for different machines.

- libslic3r/PlatePresetOverride: resolves the plate's presets and overlays
  them on the project's full config, with full_fff_config()'s precedence,
  after checking the printer is compatible (FFF, same extruder count and
  variants).
- BackgroundSlicingProcess::apply() applies it where the plate settings are
  applied; validate() reports a plate whose presets cannot be applied, and
  is_BBL_printer() follows the plate's printer.
- PartPlate / PartPlateList keep the presets per plate, give each plate its
  printer's bed, and size the plate grid to fit every bed. Without
  overrides the layout is unchanged.
- Saved in the plate metadata of the 3MF (orca_printer_preset,
  orca_process_preset), and part of undo/redo.
- Outside-the-plate checks and single-plate arrange use the plate's bed.

See docs/HLSD/per-plate-printers.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qov2bq4ZFeZHAGDRsTH8Kh
